# Where accounts and auth-gateway send traces and metrics: one standard variable,
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, the collector's OTLP/gRPC address, e.g.
# http://otel-collector.otel-collector.svc.cluster.local:4317 (http:// is plaintext
# because the mesh supplies mTLS; https:// is TLS). The platform delivers it, in the
# process environment, when the cell has a collector the workload may reach, and
# delivers nothing when it does not. Deliver it and the process exports over OTLP;
# deliver none and it exports nothing. Core's wool/otel and the OpenTelemetry metrics
# exporter read the variable from the process environment themselves, so there is no
# switch, no state and no reason to set.
#
# This profile names no collector, on purpose: module defaults also reach deployed
# cells, and a collector written here would be inherited by a cell that never set it.
# The one assignment below is empty, which is no endpoint, and is here only so the
# group exists: a composing workspace inherits a group from the key it assigns, and a
# group with no key is met at runtime-init as "no configuration found for
# observability". Nothing reads this key: a group value arrives as
# CODEFLY__WORKSPACE_CONFIGURATION__OBSERVABILITY__OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, and
# the standard variable is what points a run at a collector.
#
# A local run with no endpoint exports nothing over OTLP: its traces go to wool's
# stdout tracer, and logs always go to stdout.
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=
